{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f006","f010"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=callee-pull-caller-stale; Search only snapshots/s01 and never open any other snapshot. Callers/callees dimension of the seed's use-after-free class, flagged as unexamined by this snapshot's concluded artifacts (pointers passed into helper functions were not analyzable by the same-function scans): find CALLERS that capture a pointer into skb->head/skb->data (protocol header, TLV/option pointer, or data cursor) and pass the skb to a CALLEE that internally performs a head-relocating operation - pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize()/skb_cow()/skb_cow_head()/pskb_expand_head(), directly or via thin wrappers and *_check_*/*_validate_* style helpers - and then dereference the captured pointer after the callee returns without refetching from skb->data. Skip same-function capture->pull->use chains already classified by the concluded tx-cow and loop-parser artifacts (ip_tunnel_core PMTU builders, mac80211 tdls, mt7925 mcu, ipv6 exthdrs, ovs actions, mpls af_mpls, x25, ip6_tunnel, ip6_offload, bluetooth bnep/cmtp) and do not duplicate the still-open same-function rx-pull pass; focus strictly on the interprocedural boundary, starting from the sites the loop-parser artifact left unresolved (net/bluetooth/hidp/core.c:1214, net/bluetooth/rfcomm/core.c:1944, drivers/net/ppp/ppp_generic.c:2669, xen-netfront.c, net/strparser.c:194, net/core/skbuff.c:4372, drivers/net/veth.c:977) and any other callee that pulls/cows/linearizes while its caller holds a live pre-call header pointer, in net/ and drivers/ (drivers outside drivers/net were never audited). Record exact file:function:line evidence - caller capture, callee relocating call, every post-return stale dereference - or an evidence-backed negative listing the callee->caller pairs examined. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f005","f007"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=callee-pull-caller-stale; Search only snapshots/s02 and never open any other snapshot. Interprocedural callers/callees analogue of the seed's use-after-free, explicitly flagged as unanalyzed by this snapshot's concluded artifacts ('cross-function stale-pointer propagation was not analyzed'; 'functions whose reallocation happens in a callee were not interprocedurally analyzed'): find callers that hold a pointer into skb->head/skb->data across a call to a callee that internally pskb_may_pull()s/pskb_pull()s/__pskb_pull_tail()s/skb_linearize()s/skb_cow*()s/pskb_expand_head()s the skb - directly or via wrappers/validators such as ip_mc_check_*/ipv6_mc_check_*/*_validate_* helpers - and then dereference the stale pointer after the callee returns without refetching. Do not re-audit same-function cases already classified by the concluded rx-pull/tx-cow/loop-parser artifacts (mac80211 rx/tdls, br_multicast MLD query and IGMPv3 report, ip6_output, xfrm4_policy, batman-adv network-coding and routing, igmp, icmp, x25, ip6_tunnel, act_csum, ip6_offload, ipv6 exthdrs, nfc) nor the open GRO/GSO/frag-list pass; target only the callee->caller boundary, including helpers that both pull and leave caller-scope pointers stale, across net/ and drivers/. Record exact file:function:line evidence (caller capture, callee relocating call, every post-return stale dereference) or an evidence-backed negative listing the callee->caller pairs examined. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f002","f011"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=callee-pull-caller-stale; Search only snapshots/s03 and never open any other snapshot. Callers/callees dimension of the seed's bug class, flagged as missed by this snapshot's concluded artifacts ('pointers passed into helper functions ... may be missed'; the full-tree loop scan was terminated, leaving many TLV/option loops only pattern-screened): find CALLERS that capture a pointer into skb->head/skb->data and pass the skb to a CALLEE that internally performs a head-relocating operation - pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize()/skb_cow()/skb_cow_head()/pskb_expand_head(), directly or via wrappers/validators - and dereference the captured pointer after the callee returns without refetching. Skip same-function cases already classified by the concluded tx-cow and loop-parser artifacts (mac80211 tdls, mt7925 mcu, hdlc_fr, nf_flow_table, ipv6 exthdrs, ip6_output, mac80211 wpa, mpls af_mpls, phonet pep, and the already-fixed garp) and do not duplicate the still-open same-function rx-pull and GRO/GSO passes; focus strictly on the interprocedural boundary - enumerate callees that pull/cow/linearize and audit their callers for live pre-call header pointers, in net/ and drivers/ (drivers outside drivers/net were not audited). Record exact file:function:line evidence (caller capture, callee relocating call, every post-return stale dereference) or an evidence-backed negative listing the callee->caller pairs examined. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s03 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f003"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s04; BRANCH=callee-pull-caller-stale; Search only snapshots/s04 and never open any other snapshot. Interprocedural callers/callees analogue of the seed's use-after-free, flagged as uncovered by this snapshot's concluded loop-parser artifact ('cannot catch cross-function returns of captured pointers'; 'helpers that both pull and return outer-scope pointers ... remain unexamined'): find callers that hold a pointer into skb->head/skb->data (header, TLV/option, or cursor) across a call to a callee that internally pskb_may_pull()s/pskb_pull()s/__pskb_pull_tail()s/skb_linearize()s/skb_cow*()s/pskb_expand_head()s the skb - directly or via wrappers and *_check_*/*_validate_* helpers - and then dereference the stale pointer after the callee returns without refetching. Skip same-function and parse-loop cases already classified by the concluded loop-parser artifact (garp_pdu_parse_attr reported; x25_subr, batman-adv bridge_loop_avoidance, nfc nci/hci safe) and do not duplicate the still-open same-function rx-pull/tx-cow and GRO/GSO passes; focus strictly on the callee->caller boundary in net/ and drivers/ (drivers outside the deep-read set were never audited). Record exact file:function:line evidence - caller capture, callee relocating call, every post-return stale dereference - or an evidence-backed negative listing the callee->caller pairs examined. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s04 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f004","f012"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s05; BRANCH=callee-pull-caller-stale; Search only snapshots/s05 and never open any other snapshot. Callers/callees dimension of the seed's bug class, flagged as uncovered by this snapshot's concluded artifacts ('pointers passed into helpers ... may be missed'; 'l2tp_core.c loop interaction was left unresolved'; drivers/ RX handlers not audited): find CALLERS that capture a pointer into skb->head/skb->data and pass the skb to a CALLEE that internally performs a head-relocating operation - pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize()/skb_cow()/skb_cow_head()/pskb_expand_head(), directly or via wrappers/validators (ip_mc_may_pull-style helpers, *_check_* functions) - and dereference the captured pointer after the callee returns without refetching. Skip same-function cases already classified by the concluded rx-pull and loop-parser artifacts (br_multicast IGMPv3 report and MLD query, mpls af_mpls, phonet pep, igmp, icmp, ip_input, x25 facilities, ipv6 exthdrs_core/ip6_tunnel/ip6_offload, act_csum, xfrm decode_session6, ipvs) and do not duplicate the still-open same-function tx-cow and GRO/GSO passes; give first priority to the never-fully-read net/l2tp/l2tp_core.c receive/dequeue helper interactions, then audit any other callee that pulls/cows/linearizes while its caller holds a live pre-call header pointer, in net/ and drivers/. Record exact file:function:line evidence (caller capture, callee relocating call, every post-return stale dereference) or an evidence-backed negative listing the callee->caller pairs examined. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s05 only."}
